    {"id": "map-australia", "tier": "small", "kind": "pmtiles", "licence": "ODbL (c) OpenStreetMap contributors; Protomaps",
     "_note": "Extracted with go-pmtiles from a daily Protomaps build. Output is data (not code) and is hashed into SHA256SUMS; it cannot be pinned in advance. Protomaps deletes builds after about a week, so url is only the preferred build: when it is gone (HTTP 404), or with \"build\": \"latest\", build_kit.py uses the newest build listed in https://build-metadata.protomaps.dev/builds.json (next newest if one fails) whose tile schema major version is tiles_major (what the pinned js-basemaps style renders; bump both together). The url must be https://build.protomaps.com/<YYYYMMDD>.pmtiles. KIT-INFO.json records the build actually used (url, protomaps_build, tiles_version, requested_url, fallback); the extract cache is keyed on it.",
